What is the syntax for creating a prompt in LaTeX that asks the user to input a description of a person, including their name, age, gender, occupation, and any other relevant information? The prompt should also include a specific format for the description, such as using the word "Gegen" to indicate the opposite gender or using the phrase "request" to indicate a polite request. Here's an example of how this could be written in LaTeX:
\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Please enter the following information about a person:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textbf{PAGE}{}]
    \item Name: \textbf{[Name]}
    \item Age: \textbf{[Age]}
    \item Gender: \textbf{[Gender]}
    \item Occupation: \textbf{[Occupation]}
    \item Other relevant information: \textbf{[Other relevant information]}

    \item Please describe this person in the following format: 
        \textit{Gegen} \textbf{[Name]} (\textbf{Age}, \textbf{Gender}) - \textbf{Request} \textbf{[Other relevant information]}
\end{enumerate}
\end{document}
In this example, the prompt includes four parts: the first part asks for the person's name, followed by two pieces of information about their age and gender, respectively. The second part requests a description of the person, which includes the person's name, age, gender, and any other relevant information. The third part provides a specific format for the description, which uses the word "Gegen" to indicate the opposite gender and the phrase "request" to indicate a polite request.
The `\textit{Gegen}` command is used to italicize the person's name, while the `\textbf{}` command is used to bold the first letter of each sentence. The `\textbf{Age}`, `\textbf{Gender}`, and `Other relevant information` commands are used to insert the appropriate information into the description. Finally, the `\textbf{Request}` command is used to insert the request for a description into the prompt.
